\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces X2 on MS MARCO (1,000,000 passages; 6,200 question--subject pairs over every layout, correlation regime and selectivity). R@10: recall@10, the mean over three builds (exact settings: one). 100\%: recall@10 at the default on the uncorrelated subjects granted the whole corpus, whose filter lists every division and so passes every passage (200 pairs per build, the mean over three builds), the nearest the data come to an unfiltered baseline. QPS: one client thread through the layer, the median of three passes in the store's build-0 job, so comparable only within a row. Most search effort: the top of the store's five-level sweep. pgvector's default has iterative scans off; ``both scan limits'' raises \texttt  {hnsw.max\_scan\_tuples} to 1,000,000 and \texttt  {hnsw.scan\_mem\_multiplier} to 16 at \texttt  {ef\_search} 100; its exact search answered 998 pairs in its time. Qdrant's ACORN option has \texttt  {max\_selectivity} 1.0 and \texttt  {hnsw\_ef} 512. Ent.: recall@10 at the default on the enterprise corpus (1,468 questions; Elasticsearch's \texttt  {bbq\_hnsw}, 0.888 with \texttt  {int8\_hnsw}; Chroma on 407).}}{69}{table.caption.81}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:qual-frontiers}{{11}{69}{X2 on MS MARCO (1,000,000 passages; 6,200 question--subject pairs over every layout, correlation regime and selectivity). R@10: recall@10, the mean over three builds (exact settings: one). 100\%: recall@10 at the default on the uncorrelated subjects granted the whole corpus, whose filter lists every division and so passes every passage (200 pairs per build, the mean over three builds), the nearest the data come to an unfiltered baseline. QPS: one client thread through the layer, the median of three passes in the store's build-0 job, so comparable only within a row. Most search effort: the top of the store's five-level sweep. pgvector's default has iterative scans off; ``both scan limits'' raises \texttt {hnsw.max\_scan\_tuples} to 1,000,000 and \texttt {hnsw.scan\_mem\_multiplier} to 16 at \texttt {ef\_search} 100; its exact search answered 998 pairs in its time. Qdrant's ACORN option has \texttt {max\_selectivity} 1.0 and \texttt {hnsw\_ef} 512. Ent.: recall@10 at the default on the enterprise corpus (1,468 questions; Elasticsearch's \texttt {bbq\_hnsw}, 0.888 with \texttt {int8\_hnsw}; Chroma on 407)}{table.caption.81}{}}
