\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces X2's pre-registered statistics on MS MARCO at the stores' defaults, with 95\% intervals from a cluster bootstrap over subjects (10,000 resamples). $G$: recall@10 of uncorrelated minus negatively correlated questions at selectivities 2\% to 30\% (``gap'' needs $G \ge 0.05$, an interval above 0 and the same sign in at least four of five seeds; ``none'' $|G| < 0.02$ with the interval inside $\pm 0.03$). $D$: $|\rho _S(\text  {recall@10}, \rho _{1000})| - |\rho _S(\text  {recall@10}, \sigma _g)|$, Spearman over the 6,200 pairs (``local'' $D \ge 0.05$ with the interval above 0, ``global'' $D < 0$ with it below; n.a.: fewer than 100 pairs with recall below 1). $V$: recall@10 at 0.06\% minus the lowest at 0.5\%, 2\% and 10\%, clustered layouts, negatively correlated questions, one disjunction (``harder'', intermediate filters harder than the smallest, needs $V \ge 0.05$, an interval above 0 and four seeds; ``not harder'' $V \le 0$; the script printed these as ``U-shaped'' and ``monotone'', but $V$ does not test recovery at larger selectivities). A blank label is neither outcome. Chroma was not measured.}}{70}{table.caption.83}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:qual-x2tests}{{12}{70}{X2's pre-registered statistics on MS MARCO at the stores' defaults, with 95\% intervals from a cluster bootstrap over subjects (10,000 resamples). $G$: recall@10 of uncorrelated minus negatively correlated questions at selectivities 2\% to 30\% (``gap'' needs $G \ge 0.05$, an interval above 0 and the same sign in at least four of five seeds; ``none'' $|G| < 0.02$ with the interval inside $\pm 0.03$). $D$: $|\rho _S(\text {recall@10}, \rho _{1000})| - |\rho _S(\text {recall@10}, \sigma _g)|$, Spearman over the 6,200 pairs (``local'' $D \ge 0.05$ with the interval above 0, ``global'' $D < 0$ with it below; n.a.: fewer than 100 pairs with recall below 1). $V$: recall@10 at 0.06\% minus the lowest at 0.5\%, 2\% and 10\%, clustered layouts, negatively correlated questions, one disjunction (``harder'', intermediate filters harder than the smallest, needs $V \ge 0.05$, an interval above 0 and four seeds; ``not harder'' $V \le 0$; the script printed these as ``U-shaped'' and ``monotone'', but $V$ does not test recovery at larger selectivities). A blank label is neither outcome. Chroma was not measured}{table.caption.83}{}}
