\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces Filter size (X3): median end-to-end latency of a retrieval through the layer by the number of groups $G$ in the subject's filter, the median over three passes of 30 questions in each of five seeds (levels of 10 and 4,000 groups are in the released report). Ratio: median latency with 40,000 groups over that with one, paired by question. Recall@10 against exact search over the readable set is the same at every level unless a range (one group to 40,000) is given. Chroma's seeds 3 and 4 come from a follow-up run of the same harness on the same data, and it ran 10 questions per level because its first retrieval took more than 2\,s; ``refused'': every retrieval failed with SQLite's expression-depth error; ``crashed'': the process ended with signal 11. Images and clients are those of the conformance campaign (Appendix~\ref {sec:conf-campaign}), at default index settings.}}{73}{table.caption.90}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:qual-size}{{13}{73}{Filter size (X3): median end-to-end latency of a retrieval through the layer by the number of groups $G$ in the subject's filter, the median over three passes of 30 questions in each of five seeds (levels of 10 and 4,000 groups are in the released report). Ratio: median latency with 40,000 groups over that with one, paired by question. Recall@10 against exact search over the readable set is the same at every level unless a range (one group to 40,000) is given. Chroma's seeds 3 and 4 come from a follow-up run of the same harness on the same data, and it ran 10 questions per level because its first retrieval took more than 2\,s; ``refused'': every retrieval failed with SQLite's expression-depth error; ``crashed'': the process ended with signal 11. Images and clients are those of the conformance campaign (Appendix~\ref {sec:conf-campaign}), at default index settings}{table.caption.90}{}}
