\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {14}{\ignorespaces X5: detecting and repairing under-retrieval (GitHub Actions run 40921769714; three builds per store and corpus; every arm on every question). Recall@$k$ (R@5, R@10) and the rates are means over retrievals with $k = 10$ unless marked. Empty and Short: the answer has no hit, or fewer than $\min (k, R)$, where $R$ is what the subject may read. Trigger: the first search came back with fewer than $k$ hits, which sets off the count. Detect: the share of truly short first searches flagged \emph  {missed}; n/a: there were none; ``--'': the arm does not count. FC: false-completeness rate, the share of results marked complete that are not maximal. Latency: per-question median of three passes, end to end; ``Triggered'' is the time spent on the short result (count and repair) on triggered retrievals. Latency compares arms within one store and corpus only.}}{76}{table.caption.96}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:rep-results}{{14}{76}{X5: detecting and repairing under-retrieval (GitHub Actions run 40921769714; three builds per store and corpus; every arm on every question). Recall@$k$ (R@5, R@10) and the rates are means over retrievals with $k = 10$ unless marked. Empty and Short: the answer has no hit, or fewer than $\min (k, R)$, where $R$ is what the subject may read. Trigger: the first search came back with fewer than $k$ hits, which sets off the count. Detect: the share of truly short first searches flagged \emph {missed}; n/a: there were none; ``--'': the arm does not count. FC: false-completeness rate, the share of results marked complete that are not maximal. Latency: per-question median of three passes, end to end; ``Triggered'' is the time spent on the short result (count and repair) on triggered retrievals. Latency compares arms within one store and corpus only}{table.caption.96}{}}
