\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {16}{\ignorespaces Paired AUC of the differencing attacker, $W_1$ against $W_0^g$, pooled over the three attackers: 120, 120, 80 and 40 probes for $m = 1$, 10, 100 and 1,000 over five seeds. Above 0.5 the observable moves in the direction predicted for $W_1$ (latency up; count, recall and score down); below 0.5 it moves the other way, which serves an attacker who knows the sign just as well, so the size of a channel is $|\mathrm  {AUC} - 0.5|$. Latency values must be read against the differences between builds of identical content, which reached, per $m$, $|\mathrm  {AUC} - 0.5|$ of 0.16 for FAISS's post-filter, 0.38 for its pre-filter and 0.33 for pgvector's exact search, and 0.08 for Qdrant's exact search (Section~\ref {sec:side-results}); the other configurations were not measured that way. No correction for multiple comparisons is applied: the verdicts rest on the cells the hypotheses name, and the rest of the table is descriptive. Intervals for the cells the hypotheses name are in the text; all are in the released report.}}{81}{table.caption.108}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:side-auc}{{16}{81}{Paired AUC of the differencing attacker, $W_1$ against $W_0^g$, pooled over the three attackers: 120, 120, 80 and 40 probes for $m = 1$, 10, 100 and 1,000 over five seeds. Above 0.5 the observable moves in the direction predicted for $W_1$ (latency up; count, recall and score down); below 0.5 it moves the other way, which serves an attacker who knows the sign just as well, so the size of a channel is $|\mathrm {AUC} - 0.5|$. Latency values must be read against the differences between builds of identical content, which reached, per $m$, $|\mathrm {AUC} - 0.5|$ of 0.16 for FAISS's post-filter, 0.38 for its pre-filter and 0.33 for pgvector's exact search, and 0.08 for Qdrant's exact search (Section~\ref {sec:side-results}); the other configurations were not measured that way. No correction for multiple comparisons is applied: the verdicts rest on the cells the hypotheses name, and the rest of the table is descriptive. Intervals for the cells the hypotheses name are in the text; all are in the released report}{table.caption.108}{}}
