\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {21}{\ignorespaces Settings in the end-to-end runs (Sections~\ref {sec:e2e} and~\ref {sec:quality}). Each run is one Kaggle session, two T4 GPUs, four CPUs, 31.3\,GiB of memory; embeddings bge-base-en-v1.5, 768 dimensions, unit length. The setup scripts pin the server versions of Qdrant, Elasticsearch, OpenSearch, Weaviate, PostgreSQL's pgvector, OPA and OpenFGA; Redis comes from its package repository and the embedded stores from PyPI; the logs record the same versions in all four runs, except psycopg (3.3.8 in the seed-7 run, 3.3.6 in the repeats).}}{98}{table.caption.146}\protected@file@percent }
