\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {22}{\ignorespaces Compute of the paper's experiments; the row-level security side run (4,217\,s on Kaggle) and the vendor reproducers' short runs are not listed. Kaggle sessions have 4 CPUs and 31.3\,GiB of memory; GitHub-hosted runners have 4 virtual CPUs and 16\,GB. Jobs counts every job of the workflow run, including data, plan, report, summary and publish jobs, from GitHub's jobs API (the X7 rerun and the follow-up each include jobs the workflow skipped, one and three). On GitHub, hours sum the run times of the jobs that started; wall clock includes queueing. On Kaggle, hours are session hours, the last time stamp of each kernel log. Smoke runs that tested the harnesses, whose numbers were never analysed, and runs cancelled before they produced results are not listed.}}{98}{table.caption.148}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:app-compute}{{22}{98}{Compute of the paper's experiments; the row-level security side run (4,217\,s on Kaggle) and the vendor reproducers' short runs are not listed. Kaggle sessions have 4 CPUs and 31.3\,GiB of memory; GitHub-hosted runners have 4 virtual CPUs and 16\,GB. Jobs counts every job of the workflow run, including data, plan, report, summary and publish jobs, from GitHub's jobs API (the X7 rerun and the follow-up each include jobs the workflow skipped, one and three). On GitHub, hours sum the run times of the jobs that started; wall clock includes queueing. On Kaggle, hours are session hours, the last time stamp of each kernel log. Smoke runs that tested the harnesses, whose numbers were never analysed, and runs cancelled before they produced results are not listed}{table.caption.148}{}}
